          "id": 741813442,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, that's what I also thought. However using dwBuildNumber can get a little bit messy.\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/release-health/release-information lists all the different build numbers.\n\nFor Windows 10 we have for example 18363.1916, 19041.1387, 19042.1387, 19043.1387, 19044.1387.\nWith Windows 11 all build numbers are currently 22000.XXX\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/get-started/windows-server-release-info for Windows Server build numbers.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6518606,
            "username": "uhei",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Uli Heilmeier",
            "state": "active",
